An audit-oriented assurance runner for Rust.

mjutest connects ordinary Cargo tests with coverage routing, mutation testing through rust-mutants,
paired kill confirmation, a soundness phase, targeted fuzzing, explicit integration resources, and
reviewable repair candidates. It reports a verdict — ASSURED, DEFECT, INSUFFICIENT, ERROR — and
never a percentage.

Usage: mjutest <COMMAND>

Commands:
  verify       Verify the workspace and report a verdict
  init         Write an annotated .mjutest.toml
  plan         Say what a run would measure, without measuring it
  report       Show what a completed run concluded
  explain      Show everything a run recorded about one mutant
  accept       Record that a reviewer looked at a surviving mutant
  fix          Say what repairs a run was offered, and write the ones that hold up
  replay       Put one finding back to the tests and say whether it is still there
  trace        Read what a run recorded
  diagnostics  Bundle everything about one run into one directory
  doctor       Report the toolchain and the tools a run needs
  cache        Say what earlier runs left behind, and collect what is no longer an answer
  merge        Combine the reports of the parts of one catalog into the report the whole would have
               written
  watch        Verify again every time the workspace changes, until interrupted
  lsp          Serve what the latest run found to an editor, over the language server protocol
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Exit codes:
  0    ASSURED, CHANGE_ASSURED, SCOPE_ASSURED, PARTIAL, RESOLVED
  1    DEFECT, REPRODUCED
  2    INSUFFICIENT
  3    ERROR, invalid input, or an infrastructure failure
  130  interrupted
  143  terminated
